{"nodes": [{"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_erasure", "label": "Type erasure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most TS syntax is deleted on the way to JS. 15 lines in, 7 out: interface, type, generics, annotations, satisfies, as vanish. Runtime logic is untouched."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_erasable_vs_nonerasable", "label": "Erasable vs non-erasable syntax", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Erasable syntax describes values that already exist. Non-erasable syntax creates runtime values: enum, runtime namespace, parameter properties, legacy import=, experimental decorators."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_enum_iife", "label": "Numeric enum IIFE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "enum becomes an IIFE building a two-way map (Status.Pending=0, Status[0]='Pending'). Real object, resists tree-shaking."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_parameter_properties", "label": "Parameter properties emit assignments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "constructor(private readonly id: string) becomes field declarations plus this.id = id. private and readonly themselves are erased."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_private_erased", "label": "private is compile-time only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "private is erased; JS can read o.id. #private is the runtime-enforced form."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_as_const_replacement", "label": "as const object plus derived union", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "const Status = {Pending:'pending'} as const; type Status = (typeof Status)[keyof typeof Status]. Erasable, readable logs, same call sites."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_export_empty", "label": "export {} module marker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compiler adds export {} so a file with no imports/exports stays a module instead of a script sharing global scope."}], "edges": [{"source": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_erasable_vs_nonerasable", "target": "build_css_p2_docs_typescript_pages_phase_0_how_typescript_runs_erasure_erasure", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/typescript/pages/phase-0-how-typescript-runs/erasure.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "b